<title>USA: Beverly Enterprises sells MedView.</title>
<headline>Beverly Enterprises sells MedView.</headline>
<dateline>FORT SMITH, Ark. 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Beverly Enterprises Inc said on Monday it has completed the previously disclosed $87.5 million cash sale of its MedView Services business unit to Value Health Inc.</p>
<p>Beverly had said in October when the deal was announced that it would post a charge of $0.22 a share from the sale for accelerating the recognition of future tax expenses that had been realized as non-tax deductible goodwill.</p>
<p>On a cash flow basis, Beverly's sale of this non-strategic asset generates net after-tax proceeds totalling about $70 million.</p>
<p>Proceeds will be used to repay debt, repurchase stock or acquire selective assets, Beverly said.</p>
